Step 1 — Analyze the source code

Looking at app.py:

    The program asks for ASCII decimal 101, 101, 101 side-by-side

    ASCII decimal 101 = character 'e' (look at an ASCII table to confirm)

    The check is: if user_input == "\x65\x65\x65"

    \x65 is the hex representation of ASCII decimal 101

    So \x65\x65\x65 = "eee"

Therefore, the correct input is simply three 'e' characters: eee
Step 2 — Connect to the server

Open your terminal and run:
bash

nc candy-mountain.picoctf.net 65082

You'll see the banner and prompt.
Step 3 — Enter the correct input

When you see:
text

Send me ASCII DECIMAL 101, 101, 101, side-by-side, no space.
==> 

Type exactly:
text

eee

Then press Enter.
Step 4 — Verify it works

The program will check your input:

    If correct: prints the flag from ./flag.txt

    If wrong: shows "That wasn't it. I got: " with your input

